lse},"body":"## What\n\nDesign record for #6051: `doc/2026-11-09T05-10-38Z_design_atlas_revalidation_cadence.md` — the Atlas classification revalidation cadence under parent #6021.\n\nDecides, per the #6051 acceptance criteria (trigger table, scope per trigger, audit method with miss-rate estimate, allowlist lifecycle):\n\n- **Triggers (T1–T6)** — recognizer/rule-pack change, new source class or tier-rule change, corpus-growth threshold (≥5% / ≥1,000-chunk run, estimates), quarterly calendar round, allowlist-expiry sweep, incident/ad-hoc signal; priority-ordered with subsumption.\n- **Scope per trigger per layer** — deterministic + Tier A + pattern pack run full on T1/T4; Tier B NER runs full-internal only when Tier B inputs changed or at most annually, sampled (1,000-chunk pilot shape + 160-chunk secret sample) otherwise; vector-neighborhood and staging checks scoped per trigger. Inherits #6048 run mechanics (run_id, config_hash, 500-chunk batches, idempotent resume).\n- **Sampled human audit** — every round samples the negatives (300 internal + 160 secret sharing the #6048 calibration draw, estimates) plus a 10% dismissal re-review; rule-of-three/Wilson miss-rate bound tracked round over round, with escalation (catastrophic miss → incomplete round; >2% miss rate → full census; >10% overturn → queue re-opened).\n- **Allowlist lifecycle** — mandatory reason + expires_at (max 180d) + owner + scoped predicate; T1 suspends affected entries; T5 re-examines un-suppressed before renewal; grandfathering reported per round; no bare recognizer-wide suppressions.\n- **#6019 plug-in** — staging merge gate, new-class onboarding T2, periodic T4 gate blocking bulk backfills while incomplete, off-peak plan-spend scheduling.\n- **Dependency honesty** — #6021 has no recurrence recommendation yet; this record assumes the standing-gate branch (parent-program direction) and §8 states the one-off fallback exactly. Forks nothing from #6021; touches #6019 only at the seams; #6049/#6050 untouched siblings.\n\nSource note: the prior-art path named in the #6051 body is absent on the fleet laptop; the record is written from the body finding summary + #6021 figures + landed #6048 design and says so, per the task packet.\n\n## Tests\n\nDocs-only. `git diff --check` clean. No code tests apply (per packet).\n\nCloses #6051\n\nQueue task 13868 (lane opencode, direct).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793164&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7967&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7967&signature=efba09a4e4b99dd11f0b05fea19e50cacd676a3fffb7f10911edc85f8b301fd8\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7967?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-09T05:12:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T05:24:03Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:24:00Z","merged_at":"2026-11-09T05:24:00Z","merge_commit_sha":"f767b32ff3a7e717f99355eb411b5a4a69b672b8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/